    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91739" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῠρίτης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ,
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>in fire</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὴν τέχνην</span>, i.e. a smith, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>JConf.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sacr.</u>
				6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. λίθος</span>, a mineral <i>which
				strikes fire, copper pyrites</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.125
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				36.138
			</span></i>; other varieties of uncertain nature, ib.<i><span class="en">
				137
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHolm.</u>
				11.38
			</span></i>, Zos.Alch.<i><span class="en">
				p.120B.
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφαντον φῶς</span>
			; of a zinc ore, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.74
			</span></i>.</div>
